dir/win
description: Directory with case-insensitive filenames
- >
  On a Windows-like filesystem the filenames — hence the KEYS — are CASE INSENSITIVE: one entry
  per case-class, `Readme` and `readme` are the SAME key. With the control `.yo` subdirectory
  it becomes the overlay concrete — see the subchapter below:
- *: 00-dir_win_yo
